⚡🛢️ The IEA (international energy agency) estimates observed global oil inventories have fallen by roughly 410 million barrels since the war began, an average draw of 2.7 million barrels per day with a further 69 million barrels drawn in July alone, and it still expects a third-quarter deficit near 1.8 million barrels per day.

Aramco’s chief executive put the loss at 100 million barrels for every week Hormuz stays shut, and estimated eighteen months to refill global stocks once it reopens (meaning even after the war is over oil stocks and price will still face volatility). 

